  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oven to 450 F. Line two rimmed baking sheets with parchment paper.",
    "Stir the tomato sauce, 1 tbsp olive oil, oregano, garlic powder, sugar, and salt in a bowl.",
    "Place two flatbreads on each baking sheet. Spread about 1/4 cup sauce on each, leaving a thin border.",
    "Pat the mozzarella slices dry with a paper towel. Lay them over the sauce, dividing evenly.",
    "Bake for 10 to 12 minutes, swapping the pans halfway through. The cheese should be melted and the edges golden brown.",
    "Brush the edges with the remaining 1 tbsp olive oil. Tear the basil over the top.",
    "Let the pizzas cool for 2 minutes, then slice each into wedges and serve."
